IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-index`

-- coa24-tests-index.l4: tests for ss 1099 to 1101 (coa24-index.l4). Expected values decided from the text before the run.

§ `Tests for s 1099`

-- (2)(a), (b): UK-registered companies and unregistered companies under s 1043.
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(2)(a) a UK-registered company` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(2)(b) a body to which a provision of the Companies Acts applies by virtue of regulations under section 1043 (unregistered companies)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2)(c): overseas companies with registered particulars, other than companies that appear not to be required to have registered them.
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(2)(c) an overseas company that has registered particulars with the registrar under section 1046` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(2)(c) an overseas company that has registered particulars with the registrar under section 1046` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): every paragraph, including both paragraphs lettered (f).
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(a) a limited partnership registered in the United Kingdom (within the meaning of section 3 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(b) a limited liability partnership incorporated in the United Kingdom` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(c) a UK Economic Interest Grouping` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(ca) an EEIG establishment, within the meaning of regulation 2(1) of the European Economic Interest Grouping Regulations 1989` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(d) an open-ended investment company authorised in the United Kingdom` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(e) a society registered under the Industrial and Provident Societies Act 1965 or the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(f) first paragraph (f): a protected cell company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(f) second paragraph (f): a charitable incorporated organisation within the meaning of Part 11 of the Charities Act 2011` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099(3)(g) a Scottish charitable incorporated organisation within the meaning of Chapter 7, Part 1 of the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The lists are not closed (the Secretary of State may add bodies by order under (4)): any other body is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1099(2)-(3) the section applies to the body` `s 1099 any other body` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1): the registrar must keep the name of a body to which the section applies in the index.
#ASSERT `s 1099(1) the registrar must keep the body's name in the index` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(1) the registrar must keep the body's name in the index` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1099(1) the registrar must keep the body's name in the index` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1099(1) the index is the registrar's index of company names` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1099(1) the index is the registrar's index of company names` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1100`

-- Any person may inspect the index.
#ASSERT `s 1100 the person may inspect the registrar's index of company names` `an individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1100 the person may inspect the registrar's index of company names` `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1100 the person may inspect the registrar's index of company names` `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1100 the person may inspect the registrar's index of company names` `a partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
